= Intelligent agent — Technical =

== Agent function ==
A classical abstract agent maps percept history to action:

<pre>
f : P* → A
</pre>

where P* is the space of percept sequences and A is the action set.

Implementations approximate or realize this mapping through rules, state estimation, planning, learning, control, or combinations.

== Partial observability ==
An agent may not directly observe the complete environment state.

It can maintain internal state or beliefs inferred from observation history.

== Rational action ==
A rational-action criterion evaluates an action relative to:

<pre>
objective / performance measure
available percepts
prior knowledge
available actions
expected consequences
</pre>

Rationality does not imply perfect prediction.

